winex11: Pass the modifier keys to the drop target.

The drop target always got MK_LBUTTON as its key state, so it could
not tell a Ctrl or Shift drop from a plain one. XDND carries no
modifiers, but the X server reports them for the window under the
drag: with a drag from a Wayland client, Xwayland gives the drag
target the keyboard state, so XQueryPointer has Shift, Control and
Mod1 as the user holds them (checked against KWin 6.7).

Read them at every XdndPosition and at XdndDrop and pass them through
to DragEnter, DragOver and Drop. The button is not in the mask during
a compositor-driven drag, so MK_LBUTTON is added while dragging and
left out at the drop, as native ole32 does once the button is
released. Drivers that pass no key state keep MK_LBUTTON.
---
